  "content": {
    "id": "p39-q54-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "54",
    "prompt": "Find the minimum value of $\\dfrac1{(\\sin\\theta-3\\cos\\theta)^2}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac1{10}$.\n\nThe squared denominator has maximum $10$.",
      "worked": "Write $\\sin\\theta-3\\cos\\theta=R\\sin(\\theta-\\alpha)$. Equating coefficients gives $R\\cos\\alpha=1$, $R\\sin\\alpha=3$, so $R=\\sqrt{10}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}(\\sin\\theta-3\\cos\\theta)^2&=10\\sin^2(\\theta-\\alpha)\\\\\\frac1{(\\sin\\theta-3\\cos\\theta)^2}&\\ge\\frac1{10}.\\end{align*}$$\nEquality is attained when $\\sin^2(\\theta-\\alpha)=1$, so the minimum is $\\frac1{10}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 38
  },
